WEBVTT

00:00:04.593 --> 00:00:08.167
Traditional AI has been enhancing our lives for decades,

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:11.536
from voice assistants like Siri and Alexa to

00:00:11.536 --> 00:00:14.220
recommendation systems on Netflix and Amazon.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.352
Generative AI, or Gen AI, however, takes this a

00:00:18.352 --> 00:00:22.192
step further by crafting entirely new content,

00:00:22.192 --> 00:00:26.048
whether writing a haiku, simplifying complex concepts,

00:00:26.048 --> 00:00:30.810
or analyzing data. Gen AI is truly

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.770
a revolutionary frontier in artificial intelligence.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:38.346
Think of it as the smartest, most resourceful

00:00:38.346 --> 00:00:41.170
person you know, who is always ready to

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:45.390
assist and teach you, without ever losing patience!

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:48.594
Sound too good to be true, doesn’t it?

00:00:48.594 --> 00:00:51.290
Well, like any human, it isn’t

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:54.470
infallible and can definitely make mistakes.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:58.162
Gen AI relies on Large Language Models

00:00:58.162 --> 00:01:01.770
(or LLMs) and foundation models.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:04.001
These are neural networks trained

00:01:04.001 --> 00:01:05.790
on vast amounts of data.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.610
These model predict and generate content word by

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:13.610
word, making them capable of mimicking human creativity.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:17.282
While immensely capable, these systems are also responsibly

00:01:17.282 --> 00:01:20.278
guided by human filters, so they’ll assist

00:01:20.278 --> 00:01:23.330
with productivity rather than, say, bank heists!

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:27.270
Enter Microsoft Copilot, a tool that

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.570
brings Gen AI into the workplace.

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:34.374
Copilot is integrated directly into Microsoft 365

00:01:34.374 --> 00:01:37.766
apps like Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, and

00:01:37.766 --> 00:01:42.062
Teams, turning these familiar tools into powerhouses

00:01:42.062 --> 00:01:44.290
of creativity and productivity.

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:48.372
It works alongside you, helping draft

00:01:48.372 --> 00:01:52.764
documents, create compelling presentations, analyze complex data

00:01:52.764 --> 00:01:55.960
sets, and even craft thoughtful emails.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:59.532
However, Copilot doesn’t stop there.

00:01:59.532 --> 00:02:02.708
Its Business Chat feature connects data across apps –

00:02:02.708 --> 00:02:06.092
like emails, calendars, and chats – allowing you to

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:10.027
give natural language prompts such as, “Summarize today’s meetings

00:02:10.027 --> 00:02:12.210
and prepare a status update.”

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.338
It retrieves relevant information and

00:02:14.338 --> 00:02:17.390
generates clear, actionable responses.

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:22.930
Importantly, Copilot keeps you in control.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:25.650
It suggests ideas and content, but you

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:29.790
decide what to keep, modify, or discard.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.706
In the subsequent sections, we’ll learn more

00:02:32.706 --> 00:02:35.074
about the capabilities of Copilot, and how

00:02:35.074 --> 00:02:37.090
it can help you streamline your work.